  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zero tolerance of child labour in the granite sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arte Natuursteenbewerking B.V. purchases granite (Steel Grey) directly from her supplier who owns a quarry in India (Ballikuruva, Prakasam District, Andhra Pradesh). The supplier also owns a factory where the granite blocks are processed into slabs before being shipped to the Netherlands. Based on audit reports and research by Arisa, a non-governmental organisation (NGO), it was noted that there is a risk of child labour and other labour rights violations in the natural stone quarries where Arte is sourcing from. Arte, together with her supplier, Arisa and the local NGO MV Foundation started a so-called Child Labour Free Zone Project (CLFZ) in the area where the quarry is located. The first FBK project ran from September 2017 until April 2020; in the second FBK project this initiative is expanded to four new villages.The project targets:-	12 villages and her communities and labourers working in the quarries and processing units;-	Other supply chain actors and government officials.The project interventions consist of:1.	Setting up community structures to enhance local ownership, awareness raising, building capacity and changing social norm that every child should be in school and not at work, advocacy and monitoring, such as youth and women committees and community groups;2.	Create a Child Labour Free Zone (CLFZ) in 12 villages;	3.	Improving working conditions of (migrant)workers by training labourers and contractors and form labour groups;				4.	Engagement with the local industry association, exporters and other supply chain actors in the natural stone sector on ensuring implementation of labour rights;5.	Improve the Due Diligence system and performance of the participating companies, Arte and its supplier, through audits and dialogue.								The expected result of this project is that through integrated interventions at quarry or factory - and community level the following issues are addressed: child labour, child marriage, quality education and labour issues including occupational health and safety issues; living and working conditions of mostly migrant workers. With the goal of improving local social dialogue and formalizing labour arrangements it is expected that, in the long term, contributions are made towards the eradication of several labour abuses including child labour.</narrative>
  </description>
